Pre-requisite
---
Since I'm using `mvn` (aka Maven), make sure terminal can understand `mvn` CLI.

Instruction
---
Run `mvn test`.
Example: `\ATM-Controller>mvn test`

Should look something like below (in the terminal):
```
[INFO] Results:
[INFO]
[INFO] Tests run: 8, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0
```

Post Implementation
---
Since I assumed that there can be more than one account per each type (Checking & Saving), coming up with robust, comprehensive logic to allow user to view and select `accountId` was omitted.
This is evident in the test method that I've implemented, which could have been enhanced should I had more time.
